WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:06.210
Master Chief, the Covenant, and even energy
swords get time to shine in the series premiere

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:12.180
of "Halo," but a mysterious relic of unknown
origin might be the episode's most important

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.180
thing.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.619
Warning: spoilers ahead for "Halo" episode
1.

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:22.829
"Humanity's best weapon."

00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:28.680
After years spent in development, the official
"Halo" TV series is finally here!

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.800
The first entry in the series introduces audiences
to the world of "Halo" through the eyes of

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.680
Kwan Ha, a 16-year-old girl whose home planet
is attacked by Covenant forces.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.820
Although we spend most of the first hour with
Kwan and Spartan super soldier Master Chief,

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.550
the first chapter is also chock-full of detail
when it comes to the political affairs of

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:50.980
the "Halo" universe and the scientific research
of Dr. Catherine Halsey of the United Nations

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.050
Space Command.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:56.960
The first episode undeniably throws a lot
of exposition at both "Halo" video game veterans

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.260
and franchise newbies, so it's understandable
that some may be a little confused at the

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.550
end of the first hour.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:06.600
Luckily, if you've got a question about where
"Halo" Episode 1 leaves things, you've come

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.689
to the right place.

00:01:07.689 --> 00:01:11.340
Of course, one of the biggest questions many
fans have been asking about the "Halo" TV

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:16.290
series is the same question that has also
long haunted the video game franchise.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.960
Will we see Master Chief's face?

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.710
While the video game version of the character
has yet to reveal a complete view of what

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:27.749
lies underneath his helmet, the television
series is already taking a different approach.

00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:33.780
For the first 50 minutes of the nearly 57-minutes-long
episode, Master Chief is only ever seen with

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.299
his helmet securely fastened to the rest of
his tactical uniform.

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:41.439
Regardless of whether the warrior is in the
middle of a battle or relaxing in a spaceship,

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:45.779
Master Chief's helmet seems to be as much
a part of him as any other body part.

00:01:45.779 --> 00:01:51.459
It ultimately takes a big moment in the episode
for the legendary Spartan to bare his face.

00:01:51.459 --> 00:01:55.840
In the climax of the pilot episode, Master
Chief removes his helmet during a confrontation

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.740
with Kwan, a recently orphaned 16-year-old
girl and the sole survivor of a Covenant attack

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.740
on Madrigal.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.390
Although Kwan holds Master Chief at gunpoint,
he confidently points out that the caliber

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.940
of ammunition in her rifle wouldn't even manage
to dent his specially designed armor.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:15.980
In order to prove his loyalty to her, Master
Chief slowly lifts his helmet off his head,

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.180
leaving himself more vulnerable to attack
than we've ever seen before.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:27.400
"If you want me dead, you'll need to aim up
here."

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:32.230
Luckily for both of them, Kwan quickly decides
that Master Chief is better as an ally.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:36.750
One of the mysteries at the core of the series
so far focuses on a Covenant relic that seems

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.310
to be uniquely tied to Master Chief.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:44.150
When the super soldier first makes physical
contact with the device, a bright light emerges,

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:48.820
surprising Master Chief's fellow Spartans
and a nearby member of the Covenant.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:53.810
Even more surprisingly, however, the device
appears to trigger old memories in Master

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:54.810
Chief's head.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:59.210
While this trip down memory lane is visibly
noteworthy to the Spartan, it isn't until

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:03.810
much later in the episode that the device's
true potential is revealed.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:09.260
For reasons he is unable to fully explain,
Master Chief subsequently refuses a UNSC order

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.540
to execute Kwan.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:15.210
Realizing that a return to Reach would mean
a certain death sentence for his new traveling

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:20.510
companion, Master Chief scrambles at the last
minute to redirect his ship, but only manages

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.620
to deactivate the autopilot mere seconds before
landing.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:29.370
In response, the UNSC fires an electromagnetic
pulse at his ship, immediately grounding it.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:34.810
When all looks to be surely doomed, Master
Chief simply reaches out to the relic, triggering

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:41.290
a flurry of new memories, including what looks
to be a child's drawing of the very same device.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:46.350
More importantly, however, the device quickly
powers up the recently disabled ship, allowing

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.570
the duo to escape.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:51.170
Obviously, this raises a number of important
questions.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.780
What is the purpose of the device and who
made it?

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.960
So far, a Covenant human named Makee is the
only person other than Master Chief who is

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:02.410
able to bring it to life, obviously something
which suggests a prior relationship of some

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:03.810
sort between the two.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.260
Perhaps learning more about the origins of
this show's protagonist will also eventually

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.330
provide answers about this mysterious relic.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:15.770
Eagle-eyed viewers will notice that while
most members of the UNSC are quite unhappy

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:20.239
to see Master Chief's spaceship depart as
abruptly as it arrived, a smile appears on

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:23.620
the lips of the Spartan program leader in
the final moments of the episode.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:29.710
So, why is Halsey smiling while her multi-billion
dollar super soldier flies away with a rebel?

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:33.870
We think it probably has something to do with
the influence the Covenant relic is having

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.889
on Master Chief.

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:37.610
"I think he's having memories."

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:42.880
Although Halsey is visibly astonished at the
device's capabilities, she never seems especially

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.930
eager to see other members of the UNSC get
their hands on the device.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.820
While she admits to being somewhat worried
that Master Chief unlocking his suppressed

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:55.120
memories could produce unexpected results,
she actually does her best to cover for him

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.070
when he initially begins acting out.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:01.410
Notably, Halsey is also rather quick to suggest
solving this problem via the implementation

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:06.480
of something called "Cortana," a name that
all "Halo" video game fans everywhere will

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.040
surely recognize.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:12.590
Although she is obviously unwilling to voice
it right now, it also remains possible that

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:15.380
Halsey has ulterior motives of some form.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:20.080
In the "Halo" video games, Halsey is extremely
dedicated to the members of her Spartan program,

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.860
especially Master Chief.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.270
While it remains to be seen if the TV version
of Halsey would ever be willing to choose

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:31.070
Master Chief over the UNSC, it certainly seems
like something that will be a point of contention

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:32.360
moving forward.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:35.910
New episodes of "Halo" drop on Paramount+
every Thursday.

